"Se╔ How does this Jenkins log in? ═══════════════════════════════════════════╗──"
"  ║                                                                          ║  "
"  ║  Jenkins is behind a single sign-on proxy (oauth2-proxy) that logs in    ║  "
"  ║  through Keycloak at https://sso.example.com.                            ║  "
" J║  Issuer: https://sso.example.com/realms/acme                             ║  "
"  ║                                                                          ║  "
"  ║  Leeroy can't log in with its client "ci-proxy":                         ║  "
"  ║  device login refused: Invalid client or Invalid client credentials      ║  "
"  ║  (unauthorized_client)                                                   ║  "
" ▶║                                                                          ║  "
"  ║  Ask your Keycloak admin for:                                            ║  "
"  ║  1. A public client for Leeroy, e.g. "leeroy", in                        ║  "
"  ║  https://sso.example.com/realms/acme: client authentication off, "OAuth  ║  "
"  ║  2.0 Device Authorization Grant" on.                                     ║  "
" A║  2. oauth2-proxy accepting its tokens: --skip-jwt-bearer-tokens          ║  "
"  ║  --extra-jwt-issuers=https://sso.example.com/realms/acme=leeroy.         ║  "
"  ║                                                                          ║  "
"  ║  Enter log in: try anyway, with this issuer and client (replace Client   ║  "
"  ║  ID with the new client's once you have it)                              ║: "
"  ║  Esc close                                                               ║  "
"──╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝──"
" Enter  log in   o  open token page   Esc  close                                "
